    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2011-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "To find the number of digits, we can try to express this number in terms of powers of \\(10.\\)\n\nWe get that \\[\\begin{align*} 4^5 \\cdot 5^{10} &= 2^{10} \\cdot 5^{10} \\\\ &= 10^{10}. \\end{align*}\\]\n\nThis shows that the desired number is \\(1\\) followed by \\(10\\) zeros, for a total of \\(11\\) digits.\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Pair \\(2^{10}\\) with \\(5^{10}\\) to make \\(10^{10}\\).",
        "Rewrite \\(4^5\\) as a power of \\(2\\)."
      ],
